# Angular domain developer handbook

Business features belong exclusively in apps/{{ model.manifest.service_name }}/src/app/domains/<id>/.
The print owns platform/ (shell, auth, administration and shared infrastructure).

Read [DomainPortability.md](DeveloperReference/DomainPortability.md) for the versioned public facade, deterministic registration, dependency boundaries, session reset obligations, package/configuration requirements and migration/build proof.

Start from [DomainExample](DeveloperReference/DomainExample/README.md), copying that whole folder to domains/work-items. It is opt-in and does not introduce a backend endpoint. Keep API paths and component selectors independent of the receiving print's name.

Use standalone lazy routes, route-scoped services, OnPush components and co-located models/tests. Import platform services only through @forge/ui-contracts/v1. Avoid direct imports of another domain implementation. Clear tenant/user data on session reset and service destruction, and invalidate outstanding responses.

Run npm run build:prod, npm test -- --watch=false and npm run test:architecture before moving a domain to a compatible fresh print. The build prepares routes and navigation automatically; never edit platform route/navigation lists for a business feature.
